      "excerpt": "Ace of Tone - NUX Audio Skip to content No results PRODUCTS View All Products Amplifiers Acoustic Guitar Amps Electric Guitar Amps Bass Amps PA and Drum Amps Guitar Amp Accessories Effects Integrated Effects Multi-Effects Monarch Series Stompboxes Verdugo Series Stompboxes Core Series Stompboxes Mini Core Series Stompboxes Reissue Series Stompboxes Effects Accessories Wireless Systems Digital Wind Instrument Drums & Percussion Pianos & Keyboards Portable Digital Pianos Upright Digital Pianos Portable Keyboards MIDI Keyboard Controllers Keyboard Accessories Home Studio & Recording Accessories Lifestyle ARTISTS DISTRIBUTORS 20TH ANNIVERSARY NUX NeXt Global Guitar Contest NUX Vietnam Young Drummer Contest COMPANY PRODUCTS View All Products Amplifiers Acoustic Guitar Amps Electric Guitar Amps Bass Amps PA and Drum Amps Guitar Amp Accessories Effects Integrated Effects Multi-Effects Monarch Series Stompboxes Verdugo Series Stompboxes Core Series Stompboxes Mini Core Series Stompboxes Reissue Series Stompboxes Effects Accessories Wireless Systems Digital Wind Instrument Drums & Percussion Pianos & Keyboards Portable Digital Pianos Upright Digital Pianos Portable Keyboards MIDI Keyboard Controllers Keyboard Accessories Home Studio & Recording Accessories Lifestyle ARTISTS DISTRIBUTORS 20TH ANNIVERSARY NUX NeXt Global Guitar Contest NUX Vietnam Young Drummer Contest COMPANY Search Search Menu Ace of Tone Dual Overdrive in a Stompbox Ace of Tone Gallery / Spec / Support Dual Overdrive in a Stompbox. ACE of TONE is a dual overdrive pedal stacked with Tubeman MKII and Morning Star. Why? Because great guitarists love 2 overdrives to stack their tone. In the left corner~ Tubeman with FAT mode. Tubeman offers way more clarity and gain than any classic Tubescreamer, and we modified the circuit with a useful secondary function by simply holding the foot switch~ FAT mode. It cranks way more bass response to enhance the low-end yet makes the tone warmer! In the right corner~ Morning Star with SHINE mode. Morning Star is based on legendary Bluesbreaker circuit: very transparent, low gain drive. Like our Morning Star, it also features a simple FOOT SWITCH HOLD to engage the iconic SHINE mode. In SHINE mode, you can get way more treble sound to make your tone crystal-clear. Versatile routing and toggle switches. You can adjust the order as MS-&gt;TM or TM-&gt;MS. On the top side, you can toggle BF/TB switch for Buffer-Bypass or True-Bypass, and 9V/18V switch to 18V for internal double voltage for wider dynamic range. Control Panel Left side (Tubeman) DRIVE Knob : Controls the gain of Tubeman circuit. TONE Knob : Controls the treble frequency of Tubeman circuit. LEVEL Knob : Controls the volume of Tubeman circuit. Footswitch : Engage/disengage Tubeman circuit. Hold it for 1 second, you can turn on/off FAT mode. FAT Indicator : While you engaged FAT mode, the indicator will turn on. Right side DRIVE Knob : Controls the gain of Morning Star circuit. TONE Knob : Controls the treble frequency of Morning Star circuit. LEVEL Knob : Controls the volume of Morning Star circuit. Footswitch : Engage/disengage Morning Star circuit. Hold it for 1 second, you can turn on/off SHINE mode. SHINE Indicator : While you engaged SHINE mode, the indicator will turn on. Routing Toggle Switch : You can adjust the order from Morning Star to Tubeman or Tubeman to Morning Star. It\u2019s very useful to stack the sound. I/O Input : Connect your guitar side to INPUT jack. Output : Connect the OUTPUT signal to amp side. EXT. SW : You can use external foot controller (like NUX NMP-2) to remote this pedal. BF/TB Toggle Switch : BF means Buffer-Bypass, TB means True-Bypass. You can choose BF while you connect with several pedals in your signal chain to solve tone-loss situation. 18V/9V Toggle Switch : ACE of TONE can double the voltage internally while you toggle to 18V position, that can increase dynamic range and headroom. DC Jack Use ONLY : 9V Negative Tip power with 100mA. Feature\n- **Builder:** NUX Audio / NUX\n- **Pedal:** Ace of Tone\n- **Catalog type:** Overdrive\n- **Research level:** Surface\n- **Deep research status:** Pending\n- **Identity basis:** This page mirrors the canonical Builder + Pedal identity in `research/PEDAL_INDEX.json`. No additional technical, historical, or sonic claims are inferred here.\n\nThe Dirt Archive currently catalogs **Ace of Tone** by **NUX Audio / NUX** as a **Overdrive** pedal. This statement is limited to the archive\u2019s catalog classification. Deeper technical, historical, and sonic details remain pending verification.\n\n- No source page is recorded in the current catalog metadata.\n\n- **Archive photo:** No verified local photo is currently archived.\n- Photo provenance and validation are handled separately from this surface research record.\n\n- **Status:** Pending\n- Deeper passes will add only claims supported by exact-pedal evidence admitted by the archive\u2019s research foreman.\n\n- NUX's manufacturer page identifies Ace of Tone as a dual overdrive with two distinct drive sections.\n- The documented modes are **FAT** and **SHINE**, and the manufacturer describes the circuits as drawing from TubeMan-style and Morning Star-style overdrive voices.\n- The page documents selectable buffered-bypass / true-bypass behavior and a 9V / 18V operating selection.\n- Published specifications list approximately 9V / 100mA operation, 105 \u00d7 115 \u00d7 58 mm dimensions, and 440 g weight.\n- No circuit-clone claim beyond the manufacturer's stated design description is added.\n\n1. NUX Audio \u2014 Ace of Tone: https://nuxaudio.com/product/aceoftone/\n2. Effects Database \u2014 NUX Ace of Tone: https://www.effectsdatabase.com/model/nux/aceoftone",
